            <ArticleTitle>Renal artery embolization controls intractable pain in a patient with polycystic kidney disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>422-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 65-year-old man with adult polycystic kidney disease (APKD) and chronic renal failure suffered from intractable abdominal pain and distension for 2 weeks. Meperidine infusion did not alleviate his pain. However, pain and abdominal distension were successfully controlled by embolization of both renal arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
